==Grammar==
===Pronouns===
According to the work of Vaïsse, Peyró, Schuhmacher and Adelaar, the following schema can be proposed:

====Personal pronouns====
{| class="wikitable"
|-
!
! Singular
! Plural
|-
! 1st person
| {{lang|kuz|aqʼ}}
| {{lang|kuz|kun}}
|-
! 2nd person
| {{lang|kuz|čʼem}}
| {{lang|kuz|čim}}
|-
! 3rd person
| {{lang|kuz|a, i}}
| {{lang|kuz|ikot}}
|}
Note that {{lang|kuz|ikot}} corresponds to the relative {{lang|kuz|i}} with the plural marker {{lang|kuz|-kot}}. The forms with the added [[absolutive case]] suffix would be: {{lang|kuz|aqʼa, kuna, čʼema, čime, ia, ikota}}.

====Possessive pronouns====
{| class="wikitable"
|-
!
! Singular
! Plural
|-
! 1st person
| {{lang|kuz|aqʼsa}}
| {{lang|kuz|kunsa}}
|-
! 2nd person
| {{lang|kuz|čʼemsa}}
| {{lang|kuz|čimsa}}
|-
! 3rd person
| {{lang|kuz|isa}}
| {{lang|kuz|ikotsa}}
|}
Note that the possessive marker is the suffix {{lang|kuz|-sa}}, which is added directly to the roots of the personal pronouns.

San Román proposed a different way of marking possession, by means of prefixes added to the possessed object. The phonetic realizations are only hypothetical:

